  {
   "turn": 3,
   "action": "I hear Moss out \u2014 what exactly is he offering for the Ember?",
   "deltas": [],
   "narration": "Moss spreads his hands, easy and unhurried. \"Simple as this \u2014 you bring the Ember out past me instead of straight down to Harrow's Rest, I put silver in your palm, more than any lamplighter's wage. I don't ask how you got it open, I don't follow you home, and I don't mention your name to anyone who asks.\" His eyes flick once to Sera, weighing her, then back to you. \"That's the whole of it. I keep to my word \u2014 but only to the letter, mind.\"",
