   "narration": "You climb the stair with the Ember cradled against your chest \u2014 no flame in the lantern now, just the stone's own low red pulse lighting the hooks overhead. Moss is already there, leaning where the stair narrows, arms crossed, patient as ever. \"Settling accounts, are we?\" he says, not moving aside. \"I never asked for a promise, friend \u2014 only silver, or the stone. Name it.\" Sera's hand drops to your sleeve. \"We swore the Ember goes to Harrow's Rest,\" she says, quiet and even, counting the words like coin. \"That one I mean to see kept.\"",
